# Environment variables declared in this file are NOT automatically loaded by Prisma.
# Please add `import "dotenv/config";` to your `prisma.config.ts` file, or use the Prisma CLI with Bun
# to load environment variables from .env files: https://pris.ly/prisma-config-env-vars.

# Prisma supports the native connection string format for PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, SQL Server, MongoDB and CockroachDB.
# See the documentation for all the connection string options: https://pris.ly/d/connection-strings

# --- Core (required) ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Local development: a SQLite file path (unchanged from Phase 1).
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
#
# Production (Vercel): a Postgres connection string instead, e.g. from Neon —
# https://neon.tech (free tier, no card required). Example shape:
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DBNAME?sslmode=require"
# src/database/client.ts picks the matching driver adapter automatically based
# on this URL's scheme — see README.md's "Deployment (Vercel + Postgres)".
# Never commit a real production connection string; set it in the Vercel
# dashboard's Environment Variables instead.

# --- Phase 3D: data-source import pipeline (local/dev only — see README.md's
# "What does NOT work on Vercel") ---------------------------------------------
#
# Path to the Python venv interpreter used to spawn the racingedge_data
# import pipeline (and the "Train Baseline Model" action) from the browser
# UI. Relative paths resolve against the project root. Required for
# /data-sources' Import/Sync/Train actions to work at all; irrelevant if
# you're only using RacingEdge to browse existing data. Deliberately NOT
# computed from a path.join(process.cwd(), ".venv", ...) literal in source —
# see src/lib/pythonRunner.ts's module docstring for why that reliably
# crashes `next build` (a Turbopack build-tracer bug triggered by
# .venv/bin/python being a symlink outside the project root).
RACINGEDGE_PYTHON_BIN=".venv/bin/python"

# --- Phase 3D: Kaggle connection (optional) -----------------------------------
#
# Not normally needed — the "one-tap free setup" card on /data-sources tries
# Kaggle's public download endpoint anonymously first and only needs these if
# that's rejected (see FREE_DATA_SOURCES.md's Phase 3E section). Locally, the
# advanced CLI/Settings -> Data Connections -> Kaggle flow instead writes
# credentials to a server-only, gitignored file (.data-connections/kaggle.json)
# and sets KAGGLE_CONFIG_DIR automatically — that file-based flow only works
# in local development. On a deployment (Vercel), set these two directly as
# project environment variables instead, the same way DATABASE_URL is set —
# both the one-tap and CLI paths read them, and RacingEdge never stores
# Kaggle credentials in the database:
# KAGGLE_USERNAME=
# KAGGLE_KEY=

# --- Phase 3B: paid provider adapters (optional, NOT part of the £0 default
# path — see DATA_SOURCES.md / FREE_DATA_SOURCES.md) ---------------------------
#
# A licensed theracingapi.com subscription, for `npm run data:racingapi`.
# RACING_API_USERNAME=
# RACING_API_PASSWORD=

# --- Phase 3C: FormFav enrichment (optional, currently an honest
# non-implementation — see FREE_DATA_SOURCES.md) -------------------------------
# FORMFAV_API_KEY=
